body:
The workaround that DID work for me is just as hacky, but more complicated. I basically abandoned the built-in word wrap entirely, and instead broke the string up by word, and made a separate text node for each word. Then used the flexbox formatting to wrap them. I wrote this function to make this trick easy to utilize (and so it'll be easy to just replace this function when this bug is fixed):

```rust
pub fn wrapped_text(parent: &mut ChildBuilder, text: &str, text_style: TextStyle, align: TextAlignment, size: Size) {
	let words = text.split(" ").filter(|word| word != &"");
	parent
		.spawn(NodeBundle {
			style: Style {
				size,
				flex_direction: FlexDirection::Row,
				flex_wrap: FlexWrap::Wrap,
				align_items: match align.horizontal {
					HorizontalAlign::Left => AlignItems::FlexStart,
					HorizontalAlign::Right => AlignItems::FlexEnd,
					HorizontalAlign::Center => AlignItems::Center,
				},
				justify_content: match align.horizontal {
					HorizontalAlign::Left => JustifyContent::FlexStart,
					HorizontalAlign::Right => JustifyContent::FlexEnd,
					HorizontalAlign::Center => JustifyContent::Center,
				},
				align_content: match align.vertical {
					VerticalAlign::Top => AlignContent::FlexStart,
					VerticalAlign::Bottom => AlignContent::FlexEnd,
					VerticalAlign::Center => AlignContent::Center,
				},
				..default()
			},
			..default()
		})
		.with_children(|parent| {
			for word in words {
				parent.spawn(
					TextBundle::from_section(word, text_style.clone())
						.with_text_alignment(align)
						.with_style(Style {
							max_size: Size::new(Val::Undefined, Val::Px(text_style.font_size)),
							margin: UiRect { right: Val::Px(text_style.font_size / 4.0), ..default() },
							..default()
						})
				);
			}
		});
}
```

Credit for this idea to @jkb0o's comment in #1490.
